---
import CtaBlock from "../components/CtaBlock.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import RelatedLinks from "../components/RelatedLinks.astro";
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { buildMeta, organizationSchema } from "../lib/seo";

const meta = buildMeta({
  title: "About Harmless Apps | A calmer digital world for kids",
  description:
    "The philosophy behind Harmless Apps: building kids apps designed to be calmer, clearer, and less chaotic.",
  pathname: "/about/"
});
---

<BaseLayout {...meta} schemas={[organizationSchema()]}>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="About"
    title="A calmer digital world for kids"
    intro="Harmless Apps is a simple brand direction built around one idea: if families use screens sometimes, those experiences can be designed with more restraint."
    tags={["philosophy", "calm-first", "less chaotic", "kids apps"]}
  />

  <section class="content-block">
    <div class="shell narrow prose">
      <p>
        The phrase harmless apps is intentionally modest. It does not suggest
        that apps are neutral by default or that one product can solve the whole
        screen-time problem. It suggests a bar: make digital products that are
        easier to live with.
      </p>
      <p>
        In practice, that means fewer manipulative loops, fewer interruptions,
        and a stronger respect for the child, the parent, and the moment after
        the device is put away.
      </p>
      <p>
        <a href="/apps/dennys-maze/">Denny's Maze</a> is the first concrete
        example on the site. It uses maze play because mazes naturally support
        quiet focus and simple completion without requiring fast, flashy reward
        patterns.
      </p>
      <p>
        This philosophy is not anti-fun and not anti-screen. It is pro-restraint.
        It assumes that a kids app can be engaging without acting like a casino,
        a cartoon feed, or a behavior trap.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <RelatedLinks
    links={[
      {
        href: "/apps/dennys-maze/",
        title: "Denny's Maze",
        description: "See the product that anchors this philosophy."
      },
      {
        href: "/screen-time-without-overstimulation/",
        title: "Screen time without overstimulation",
        description: "A parent-facing version of the same idea."
      },
      {
        href: "/faq/",
        title: "FAQ",
        description: "Short answers about claims, age fit, and intent."
      }
    ]}
  />

  <CtaBlock text="If the philosophy makes sense, Denny's Maze is the easiest place to see it in product form." />
</BaseLayout>
